brotli-dec-wasm@2.3.2 (vendored decoder-only build)
https://www.jsdelivr.com/package/npm/brotli-dec-wasm
https://www.npmjs.com/package/brotli-dec-wasm
Dual licensed: MIT (see LICENSE-MIT.txt) or Apache-2.0

Vendored files:
  pkg/brotli_dec_wasm.js       wasm-bindgen ESM glue (9.4 KB)
  pkg/brotli_dec_wasm_bg.wasm  brotli decoder (208 KB)
  loader.js                    ES module wrapper; exposes self.brotliReady /
                               self.brotliDec to the classic scripts

Why vendored: WOFF2 is brotli-compressed. Firefox 147+ and Safari 18.4+
provide DecompressionStream('brotli') natively and are used first;
Chrome/Edge do not ship it yet, so this decoder is the fallback.

How to update:
  1. Check the latest version at
     https://www.jsdelivr.com/package/npm/brotli-dec-wasm
  2. Download straight from jsdelivr and overwrite the vendored copies:
       https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/brotli-dec-wasm@<version>/pkg/brotli_dec_wasm.js
       https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/brotli-dec-wasm@<version>/pkg/brotli_dec_wasm_bg.wasm
       https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/brotli-dec-wasm@<version>/LICENSE-MIT.txt
     or install in a scratch dir and copy from node_modules:
       bun add brotli-dec-wasm@<version>
       cp node_modules/brotli-dec-wasm/pkg/* pkg/
  3. If the exported API changed, update loader.js to match: it loads the
     default export (async init) and exposes the whole module namespace
     (incl. the DecompressStream class) as self.brotliDec, which the
     fallback path in resolve.js consumes.
  4. Bump the version on the first line of this README.
  5. Verify: open the inspector on a page that loads woff2 fonts, expand
     the "Resolved Names" section and confirm rows resolve.
